1. What are you responsible for in your block when it comes to deadlines and announcements?

As a block representative, I am responsible for sharing important announcements, deadlines, schedules, and reminders with my blockmates. I also make sure that the information from our instructors reaches everyone in the block.

2. Who else posts deadlines or announcements besides you (instructors, other students)?

Aside from me, our professors, instructors, and block advisers also give announcements and important reminders. Sometimes, the Mayor of KB and other student representatives also share information that may be relevant to our block.

3. Where do you post or relay announcements (group chat, MOLE, in class)?

Most of the time, I share announcements through our Group chat because it is the easiest way to reach everyone. Sometimes, I also relay important information personally or during class.

4. How do you find out about a deadline or schedule change in the first place?

I usually get the information directly from our Professors, through class discussions, group chats, or Gchat. I make sure to understand the announcement first before sharing it with my blockmates.

5. Do you ever have to repeat or correct an announcement? How often?

Yes, especially when some blockmates do not see the announcement right away or when there are changes in the schedule. Sometimes, I need to repeat the information to make sure everyone is informed.

6. Can you recall a time when a deadline was missed, wrong, or changed late? What happened?

There are instances when deadlines or class schedules change unexpectedly, usually because of adjustments made by our professors or instructors. Whenever this happens, I make sure to inform my blockmates immediately and share the updated details in our group chat. Sometimes, it causes confusion, especially for those who have already planned their schedules or started working on their requirements based on the previous announcement.

7. Have there been weeks when many requirements were due at once? How did your block handle it?

Yes, especially during midterms and finals. There are times when different subjects have activities, projects, and deadlines at the same time. As a block, we try to remind one another and manage our time properly. We also help each other by sharing important information.

8. Imagine a shared board where your block lists all its deadlines in one place. How would you want to add or update entries?

I think it would be helpful if the shared board were simple and easy to use. I would like to add the subject, activity, deadline, and important reminders. It should also be easy to update whenever there are changes so everyone can see the latest information.

9. Would you want classmates to be able to add or correct entries, or only you?

I would prefer that blockmates can also add or suggest corrections, but there should still be someone responsible for checking and confirming the information. This way, everyone can participate, and we can avoid incorrect announcements.

