BLOCK REP
* What are you responsible for in your block when it comes to deadlines and announcements?
   I serve as the central point of contact between instructors and my blockmates. My main responsibility is making sure all official class announcements, project specs, exam schedules, and submission deadlines are clearly communicated, double-checked, and easy for everyone to find.
 * Who else posts deadlines or announcements besides you (instructors, other students)?
   Instructors usually post official announcements on MOLE or course channels, but key updates also come directly through individual subject representatives, team leads for group projects, or classmates who ask for clarification during/after lectures.
 * Where do you post or relay announcements (group chat, MOLE, in class)?
   I primary relay updates in our official Messenger group chat, pin critical announcements at the top of the chat, and occasionally reiterate urgent reminders verbally right before or after in-person classes.
 * How do you find out about a deadline or schedule change in the first place?
   Usually directly from the instructor during class, via email/MOLE notifications, or through messages sent to me by professors or subject reps asking me to inform the class.
 * Do you ever have to repeat or correct an announcement? How often?
   Yes, quite often. Questions come in frequently when deadlines shift or instructions on MOLE conflict with what was said in class. I end up re-clarifying details or bumping pinned messages multiple times a week as submission dates approach.
 * Can you recall a time when a deadline was missed, wrong, or changed late? What happened?
   Yes—there have been instances where an instructor verbally extended a deadline or moved a submission time late at night without updating the portal right away. It caused confusion over whether the system would lock, requiring me to reach out directly to the instructor to confirm and reassure the block.
 * Have there been weeks when many requirements were due at once? How did your block handle it?
   Definitely, especially around midterms and finals when major machine problems, lab reports, and project demos converge. As a block, we try to map out the heavy days, prioritize task order together, and sometimes request reasonable extensions from instructors when multiple major deliverables overlap on the exact same day.
 * Imagine a shared board where your block lists all its deadlines in one place. How would you want to add or update entries?
   I’d want a fast, low-friction input—like typing a quick quick-entry form or command (title, subject, due date/time, and link) that instantly populates the board, along with a simple edit/tag system to flag status changes like "Extended" or "Pending Clarification."
 * Would you want classmates to be able to add or correct entries, or only you? Why?
   A hybrid model works best: allow classmates to submit or suggest additions/edits (especially for subject-specific tasks), but give block reps moderation approval rights. That way, the workload of keeping it updated is shared without risking accidental deletion or unverified information being posted as official.
